# === Framework-only publication ===
# Publish the REUSABLE FRAMEWORK only: .kiro/skills, the generic .kiro/steering, and the guides.
# NEVER publish a real case (sources) nor any generated deliverable (they carry case content:
# system names, architecture, threat scenarios). See PUBLISHING.md and the project-context steering
# (data classification: threat/vuln details stay internal).

# --- Real source material (confidential, read-only to the skills) ---
sources/

# --- Generated deliverables (per-project output folders) ---
# Every skill writes its deliverables under output/${project_name}/ (see the output-convention
# steering). These are real, project-specific outputs (system names, architecture, threat
# scenarios) - never framework material, never published. Pattern-based, so it covers every
# project's folder without naming any.
output/

# --- Agent scratch / transient work files ---
.kiro/.temp_ai/

# --- Frozen copy of any inherited third-party pattern (not ours to publish) ---
reference/

# --- Project-specific specs (describe a REAL case, not the generic framework) ---
# A spec under .kiro/specs/ names a concrete application and carries project decisions, so it is
# case material, not reusable framework. Exclude every spec by default (pattern, not by name).
# If you ever author a spec that is genuinely GENERIC framework material, allow-list it explicitly
# with a negation (e.g. `!.kiro/specs/<generic-spec>/`).
.kiro/specs/*/

# --- Personal / project pilotage steering (NOT reusable framework) ---
# Any steering file that carries personal identity, team attribution, roadmap, undecided
# governance choices or internal paths is pilotage, not framework. Keep it local, never publish.
# Pattern-based so it catches any such file, whatever its exact name:
#   - *.local.md / *.perso.md     -> explicit "do not publish" marker you can add to any steering
#   - project-context*.md         -> the filled, case-specific context (the *.template.md stays)
# The generic, publishable steering (command-execution, office-*, skill-authoring) is NOT matched.
.kiro/steering/*.local.md
.kiro/steering/*.perso.md
.kiro/steering/project-context.md
.kiro/steering/project-context.*.md
# Keep the depersonalized template that ships WITH the framework:
!.kiro/steering/project-context.template.md

# --- Legacy deliverables left at the REPO ROOT (pre output/ convention) ---
# New deliverables go under output/${project_name}/ (excluded above). Older ones may still sit at
# the bare project root (the framework does not move existing files). The belts below keep those
# out of the repo too, by file type and by optional prefix.
# Optional prefix belt: uncomment and set it to your ${project_name} (the prefix every skill uses
# for its outputs), e.g.:
#   my-app_*
# <project_name>_*

# --- Belt-and-braces: exclude deliverable file types at the REPO ROOT only ---
# (never ship a generated office doc / diagram / model json / produced deck from the root;
#  real example-free framework assets live under .kiro/skills/.../assets, not at the root)
/*.pptx
/*.docx
/*.xlsx
/*.xlsm
/*.drawio
/*_README.md
/*_model.json
/*.model.json

# --- OS / editor noise ---
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*~
*.tmp
*.tmp_*

# =============================================================================
# OPTIONAL: PUBLIC-REPO MODE  (OFF by default - see PUBLISHING.md, decision R2)
# =============================================================================
# The skills bundle official, internal company templates/standards under
# `.kiro/skills/**/assets/` (reference models, standard documents, architecture
# patterns). Whether those binaries may leave an internal repo is a HUMAN decision
# (public vs restricted). This block lets you switch to a "public-safe" tree WITHOUT
# editing every skill: uncomment it to exclude the bundled binary assets, then follow
# PUBLISHING.md to drop a placeholder README in each `assets/` folder explaining which
# official file to obtain and where to put it. Leave commented for an internal/restricted
# repo that ships everything.
#
# .kiro/skills/**/assets/templates/*.docx
# .kiro/skills/**/assets/templates/*.xlsx
# .kiro/skills/**/assets/templates/*.xlsm
# .kiro/skills/**/assets/templates/*.pptx
# .kiro/skills/**/assets/templates/*.pdf
# .kiro/skills/**/assets/templates/*.drawio
# .kiro/skills/**/assets/*.pdf
# # Keep the placeholder READMEs that tell a cloner what to drop back in:
# !.kiro/skills/**/assets/**/README.md
Exemples/